From ee9d05981357a27335e1982c1686262e7bc39cc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chau Ly <chaul@amperecomputing.com>
Date: Tue, 31 Oct 2023 07:16:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] intrusionsensor: Initial value read for GPIO type

The GPIO-typed intrusion sensor has been using interrupt to acknowledge
the toggling of the gpio and reading value only when the gpio is
toggled. This is good so far but requires an initial reading of value to
set the first value to D-Bus, otherwise it would only be updated when
the gpio flips its state and miss the assert event if the first value is
not Normal.

This commit lets GPIO-based sensor have initial value reading after the
first call to pollSensorStatus() in its overridden start() method. In
order for the initial update to have effect on DBus, move the DBus
interface initialization to the constructor of the base class.

This commit also defines the pollSensorStatus function in the base class
to use timer polling method and sets it as virtual so it can be
overridden by the GPIO class and directly used by the others.

Tested on Ampere's Mt.Mitchell platform.

1. GPIO type: the sensor successfully shows its initial state on D-Bus,
and reacts to the toggling of the GPIO correspondingly.
2. The other two types work normally.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/67465]

Signed-off-by: Chau Ly <chaul@amperecomputing.com>
Change-Id: If8cc394b01c85d48f5d8f8ad625ef87f2036f0ab
---
